    "text": "The Acquedotto dell'Acqua Vergine, also known as Aqua Virgo, is an ancient Roman aqueduct that supplied water to Rome from 19 BC and remains a vital source of drinking water today. Its engineering, longevity, and the iconic fountains it feeds make it a key element of Rome’s urban heritage.",
